## 5. Suggested way to internalize this

A useful mental model: sort each of the ten sources along two axes â€”

```
                    Structurally complete
                            ^
         crt.sh  â€¢          |
                             |          â€¢ Shodan (for scanned hosts)
   DNS records  â€¢            |
                             |
Sample-based/indexed <-------+-------> Historically archived
                             |
      theHarvester â€¢         |          â€¢ Wayback Machine
                             |
        GitHub search â€¢      |     â€¢ WHOIS (registry, not content)
                            Sparse/incomplete
```

Thinking in terms of *what kind of gap* each source fills (rather than
memorizing tool names) makes it much easier to reason about which source
to reach for, and how much to trust a given result.
